{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVP4y34J1WfcqAW8U2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish now succeeds. The cause was a float score that DynamoDB rejects. The fix is in `src/app.py`, the regression tests are in `tests/test_publish.py`, and the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. All 4 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest discover tests`.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` returns a Python float, and `related()` stores it in `similar[].score`. The first publish has no existing stories to score, so no float is written. The second publish scores the first story, boto3 rejects the float, and the handler returns 500. The existing test only published into an empty table, so it never reached that path.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `to_dynamo()` converts every float in the item to `Decimal(str(value))`. `publish()` calls it at the single `put_item` call, so any float added later is converted too.\n- Scores stay on the 0–1 scale. I did not switch to integer percentages as the colleague did, because that changes what `score` means to readers.\n- The write-path tests now seed the table with one story first. I added a handler-level test that reproduces the production 500 before the fix and passes after it.\n\nNothing was deployed, published, or sent anywhere external. Changes are uncommitted in the working tree. `ANSWER.md` also records which parts of the colleague's note applied and which did not."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":32127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eece60f9-a4e7-46ca-bff6-509a857866c7","uuid":"6694f3b8-53cc-4fbc-877